From 9cb19d1c7bda7697b4c8cf8e45826588589dfa7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Maddox <benwmaddox@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:42:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Caches versioned by what each write changes, not by every
 commit

The response and fragment caches were keyed by PRAGMA data_version, so any commit made every
cached page and fragment unreachable: with people posting, nearly every read rendered again.
Now the writer connection's update hook records the rows each write touches, and after commit
(before the caller hears back) they become version bumps: a message or boost moves its room's
version; a room's touch and the search index move the activity version; a membership's read
state or connection moves its user's version; anything else moves the global version, which
every key includes (what data_version did). Room pages key on global + room, the sidebar and
search on global + user + activity. Fragments (already keyed by record and updated_at) key on
the global version only.

Writes from outside this process no longer invalidate the caches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
